# Mail-related application logs on nimbini (created 2026-08-27).
#
# rotate 0 and no compression are DELIBERATE and follow the policy set for
# practiceforge-phi: these logs can carry the titles, senders, recipients or
# content of practice email. Retaining gzipped archives would mean keeping
# compressed copies of that indefinitely. Rotation here DELETES.
#
# Scope is every mail log, not only the obviously-COHS ones. mailforge covers
# COHS and Napier both, and Napier practice mail is clinical data too. The risk
# is asymmetric: rotate 0 on a PHI-free log costs only lost history, whereas
# ordinary rotation on a PHI-bearing one leaves patient data in .gz files. So
# the whole class gets the strict rule rather than relying on a classification
# that could be wrong.
#
# copytruncate is REQUIRED, not stylistic: these services write via systemd
# StandardOutput=append:, so systemd holds the file open. A plain rename would
# leave the service writing to an unlinked inode and the new file would stay
# empty forever. Same reasoning as practiceforge-phi.
#
# create 0600 will will — all seven of these were mode 644 (world-readable)
# until 2026-08-27 and were chmod'ed then. Do not let rotation restore a
# permissive mode.
#
# History cleared 2026-08-27: mail-sync.log (17.5 MB, last written 2026-05-04)
# truncated. Rotation exists so that clearance is not a one-off.

/home/will/.local/share/gmpull.log
/home/will/.local/share/mail-sync.log
/home/will/.local/share/mailforge.log
/home/will/.local/share/cohs-trash-mover.log
/home/will/.local/share/mailcurator-drift.log
/home/will/.local/share/gmail-push-tags.log
/home/will/.local/share/gmail-push-tags-watchdog.log
{
    size 5M
    rotate 0
    copytruncate
    missingok
    notifempty
    create 0600 will will
}
